      "writtenOn": "2018-02-12T04:27:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Does power_button_pulse_enabled control \u0027power button SMI pulse\u0027?\n\nYes, power_button_pulse_enabled controls the pulse from EC to AP (L278 in this file).\n\n\u003e And doesn\u0027t set_pwrbtn_to_pch(0,0) assert the power button\n\nYes, set_pwrbtn_to_pch asserts the power button to the PCH. I wrote the comment using negative connotation because power_button_pulse_enabled is enabled by default. What I meant by the comment \"If power button SMI is disabled, then it should be honored.\" is --\u003e Do not assert power button when power_button_pulse_enabled is disabled by AP. But, I understand that the comment could be a little confusing. I can update it to \"enabled\" if that sounds correct.",
